course: dictionary
lesson: 375
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). To choose the right meaning, look at the context: the other words and sentences around it. «Anvil» is one of these words.
explain: «A tuskfish carries a clam in its mouth and smashes it on a rock, using the rock as an anvil.» The clues are smashes and rock. A fish is not a blacksmith, so anvil here means a hard surface that you hit something against.
explain: Now read «The blacksmith hit the hot metal on the anvil.» The clues are blacksmith and hot metal, so anvil means the heavy iron block. Ask yourself: what is the sentence about? The topic often tells you the meaning.
explain: Other clues work the same way. «The ear has three tiny bones: hammer, anvil and stirrup.» The clue is ear, so anvil is a tiny bone. The phrase «anvil cloud» tells you the meaning is the flat top of a thundercloud. Check your choice by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: One word can have more than one meaning, so always check the context.
fact: «Anvil» means a heavy iron block with a flat top, where a blacksmith hammers hot metal into shape.
fact: «Anvil» can also mean a tiny bone in the middle ear, also called the incus.
fact: «Anvil» can mean the flat, spreading top of a big thundercloud, as in «anvil cloud».
fact: Animals can use a hard stone as an anvil, the same way a blacksmith uses an iron block.
exercise: «The blacksmith hammered the horseshoe on the anvil.» What is an anvil here? | *A heavy iron block with a flat top | A metal tool for cutting | A tiny bone in the ear | The flat top of a thundercloud
exercise: «A tuskfish smashes its clam on a rock, using the rock as an anvil.» What does anvil mean here? | *A hard surface to hit something against | A tiny bone in the ear | A dark storm cloud | A tool for cutting metal
exercise: The ear has three tiny bones: hammer, anvil and stirrup. Which meaning of anvil is this? | *A tiny bone in the middle ear | A cloud top | A stone a thrush uses to crack shells | A block where a blacksmith works
test: In the phrase «anvil cloud», what does anvil mean? | A tiny bone in the ear | *The flat, spreading top of a big thundercloud | A heavy iron block for hammering metal | A stone used to crack shells
test: In «The smith struck the glowing iron on the anvil», which clue shows that anvil means a blacksmith's block? | *The glowing iron and the smith | The word the | The word on | The word struck
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Sound passes to the inner ear through the anvil, a tiny bone in the middle ear»? | A stone a bird uses to crack shells | A heavy iron block for a blacksmith | *A tiny bone in the middle ear | The top of a big thundercloud
